            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Recent statistics from the Patients Association show 17 per cent of patients raised poor pain relief as a concern in calls to its helpline. In the third of our four-part series examining the four strands of fundamental care, we look at how competing demands can affect effective pain relief and how some organisations have made improvements.</AbstractText>
